_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Default extraction is over-broad for body destructuring.**

Both paths collect defaults from any object destructuring in the function body, even when unrelated to `props`. This can leak unrelated defaults into prop docs.



<details>
<summary>💡 Narrow collection to props-derived destructuring</summary>

```diff
-        for (const varDecl of stmt.declarationList.declarations) {
-          if (typescript.isObjectBindingPattern(varDecl.name) && varDecl.initializer) {
-            collectBindingDefaults(typescript, varDecl.name, defaults, checker);
-          }
-        }
+        for (const varDecl of stmt.declarationList.declarations) {
+          if (!typescript.isObjectBindingPattern(varDecl.name) || !varDecl.initializer) {
+            continue;
+          }
+          const init = varDecl.initializer;
+          const firstParamName =
+            typescript.isIdentifier(firstParam.name) ? firstParam.name.text : undefined;
+          const fromProps =
+            firstParamName &&
+            ((typescript.isIdentifier(init) && init.text === firstParamName) ||
+              (typescript.isCallExpression(init) &&
+                init.arguments.some(
+                  (a) => typescript.isIdentifier(a) && a.text === firstParamName
+                )));
+          if (fromProps) {
+            collectBindingDefaults(typescript, varDecl.name, defaults, checker);
+          }
+        }
```
</details>


